\noindent\underline{\textsf{Philosophy of our proof}}
$\newline$

\emph{Inspired by \cite{lie2015triangle}, our intention is to show that even in the variable case, the operator
$$T_{j(x),m}\:\:(\textrm{or equivalently}\:\:B_{j(x),m})\,$$
obeys similar decay bounds with $T_{j,m}$ which can be extracted from the corresponding bounds for the $j(x)=j$ constant case. In other words, one can identify a unified approach that deals simultaneously with both the bilinear Hilbert transform and the maximal operator along non-flat curves.}

